{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the serpent was cunning.</b> What has this to do here? It should have been juxtaposed to ״וַיַּעַשׂ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהִים לְאָדָם וּלְאִשְׁתּוֹ כָּתְנוֹת עוֹר וַיַּלְבִּשֵׁם.״ Rather, it teaches you from what plan the serpent sprang upon them: he saw them naked and engaged in relations in the open, and he coveted her." "<b>Cunning of all.</b> According to his cunning and greatness was his downfall — cunning of all, cursed of all (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Though He said, etc.</b> Perhaps He said to you, 'You shall not eat of all,' etc. And even though he saw them eating of the other fruits, he piled up words against her so that she would answer him and he would come to speak about that tree."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:28.791913219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}